    "description": "144 Locksley Ave is a charming 3-story residential fourplex located in San Francisco's desirable Forest Knolls District. \u00b1 2,580 SF building on a \u00b1 3,062 SF lot, built in 1961. The property contains two units of 1 bedroom &1 bathroom and two units of 2 bedrooms &1 bathroom. The first floor is a spacious 4-car garage with laundry area. The second floor has one 1 bedroom unit and one 2 bedrooms unit, the third floor has a similar layout as the second floor. One 2 bedrooms unit is vacant now and will be delivered vacant at close. Current monthly rents are $1,620.28, $1,285.22, $1,865.03, and the vacant unit pro forma rent will be $3,200. Tenants pay for their own electricity and internet/cable; seller pays water, trash, and the main water heater gas. Good maintenance and long-term tenants. The property is located in the southwestern part of San Francisco, walking distance to the University of California San Francisco Parnassus Campus. It is highly attractive to the nearby medical professionals and students. Forest Knolls District resides at the foothills of Mount Sutro Reserve. Residents are surrounded by luscious woods and enjoy the tranquil environment with a convenient urban life. Close to West Portal, which is a delightful shopping district that with a collection of stores, including bookstore, hardware store, markets, thrift boutiques, various restaurants, library, and a movie theater. If you like hiking, Mount Sutro has miles of trails also the closely famous Golden Gate Park and Botanical Garden. The property is just around 4 miles from Downtown San Francisco amenities. Such a great real estate asset for expending your investment portfolio or lives in one of the units. Sold in \u201cAs-Is\u201d condition. Drive by only, do not disturb or talk to tenants. Offer subject to interior inspection."
  },
